# gh #51 (docs/20 U26) regression: G0 slips mid-sentence. Before the fix the memo ended the
# moment G0 read up once (a memo ended and the next began 0.82 s later). Now a let-go G0
# records on through a 0.6 s grace and the page says so; pressed again inside it, it is
# the same memo (one Start, one file); only a grace that runs out ends it, saved.
# The grace counts toward rec_min_ms: a hold let go 0.2 s after ● REC is still too short.
boot store=sd usb=on bat=4100 lang=zh
include ../common/demo_state.cpas
wait 1000
down g0
wait 600
mic 2500 speech
shot held  G0 held, talking: Voice memo, hint "[G0]let go: stop"
up g0
mic 200 speech
shot slipped  Let go 0.2 s: still recording, yellow capsule "Let go · hold within 0.6 s"
down g0
mic 2000 speech
shot pressed-again  Pressed again: the same memo records on, the timer unbroken
up g0
wait 400
shot grace-again  Let go again 0.4 s: still in the grace
wait 300
shot ended  No press within 0.6 s: ended, "Recording saved · 0:05"
wait 2600
shot home  Back on Home: R1, only one
# a short hold: 0.7 s in all, the grace and all under 1 s of audio
hold g0 700
wait 900
shot short  Held 0.7 s, then let go: after the grace "Too short: discarded"
wait 2600
